<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10196"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 4:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about a new way of looking at this puzzle. A third grader could have made it the way we have been interpreting it. Try doing it as a letter path, as long as your pencil follows the path, you can go any direction, up, down, across, or diagonal.  <BR> <BR>MO Grid:mull, snit, mis pig,mame, dl, dl, sit, jello, jef, leo, ciophn, six, wit, pet, hint, slit, tip, det, ht, poet, fog, your it, builds, lie, fume, jr, fox, foe, fib, nanci, then, nestle, jew,tub, tempt, toll, poll, poem, salt, hated, peot, pest, limits, sir, nanci, senor, retch, roe, ted, ten, tit, cia, dike, depth, rib, quills, unlit, slip, juke, kiss, kids, kiddo, loot, nola, jig, praise o pj, crass, flown, fib, vd, dl, sin, rat, spated, ted, dl, my four, craft, sale, hex, own, pow, two, oasis, few, im so, fall, fall, tag, stag, path, slit, pub, jails, fanci, raspy, met <BR> <BR>ID Grid:pew, hiv, north, recoil, con, condit, shag, tear, dea, sue, ice, hones, DER son, dean, padre, step, steph, pond, sold, sob, nephew, soffi, lucy,nest, nail, dear radre, rail, rear, hero, coat, cop, read, folk, lion, front, splash, gift, shiv, fray, que, steal, fob, lean, him , her, slander,quest, snag, w&#42;ore, den, adt, dig, pray, dr, prayer, doll, dcf, VI, sos, helm, hornet, respond, wag, wage, whet, radre, con, ties, tied, tiarra, dim, boo, hoo, sue, bold, rx <BR> <BR>Ruse Grid:leo, ceo, lane, poet, more, pore, teen, fist, fir, sister, dame, wear, dress, mace, tpm, rice, race, narc, nest, empty, slut, roar, were, camera, camera, steer, dig, ice, hope fades, six, fuse, god, shed, photo, joe, pjs, pelt, pent, fat, far, begin, sled, damn, dancer, fog, lust. leaf, toes, steal, splat, splash, knee, rein, rein, svu, oj or jo, mopes, sad, five, success, seance, cancer , reel, rest, lose, oh, rant, hark, her, ford, ruser, ask, steer, sad, grope, ode, road, rodeo, dine, dingy, post, stale, hell, hose, meet, carrot, warn, vian, nance, nam, naive, dork, bath, used, stash, seal, modas. <BR> <BR>Well, this many words cant be a coincidence. Remember, we got fooled before because we only saw the obvious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
