<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10571"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 1:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, he also gave us WICHITA &#40;ATIHCIW is what I do when catching cold&#41;; POI; &#34;Officer Rader;&#34;  Strong; &#34;Larry Anderson&#34;&#60;?&#62;; Ran help; and, as mentioned, a wonderfully entrapped MY DNA inside HANDYMAN.   I&#39;d go on but seem to be at a TY UP. <BR> <BR>I am of the opinion that there is no &#34;ulterior code&#34; happening here - unlike Zodiac&#39;s ciphers.  Just some hidden words, not a truly complex puzzle to leave, after all.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10571-->
<!--Post: 10836--><!--Time: 1110248199-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10836"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 6:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree, J_eric - no fancy stuff at all.  I&#39;ve dumped some of his strings &#40;both known and possible BTK&#41; into a couple of programs and ended up just shaking my head at myself for wasting the time.  I liked how Wichitaboy culled out the obvious keyboard traversal filler on the main puzzle, but what was left was junk.  All that seemed left to me was a rather dopey &#34;I AM CLD DL&#34; - no risky clues there.  The only clue that matters in this game is DNA &#40;and I&#39;m not talking 3 letters in a puzzle&#41;.  On another board, MissCalculation &#40;love the name&#41; picked all kinds of 2-D wordfinds out of the puzzles, but it was obviously just random stuff.  If the more enigmatic string posts have any meaning &#40;or if they&#39;re BTK&#39;s at all, which I seriously doubt!&#41;, then I&#39;m figuring they&#39;re either anagrams &#40;uncertain, multi-solution, and low-value&#41; or huge acronyms &#40;even more worthless&#41;.  I think I saw a solution to one of them that involved cycling through the letters &#40;4-4-0&#41;, but if that was our boy Denny, I&#39;ll lick my calculator clean.  But I do think the &#40;in my opinion&#41; likelihood that there&#39;s no substitution going on in genuine BTK stuff makes it more likely that a simple solution is going to be a hit.  That&#39;s why I&#39;m intrigued by the values 7 and 14 in the more recently released March &#39;04 &#40;&#34;baby&#34;&#41; puzzle, which like the big puzzle is genuine BTK.  If it&#39;s an anagram, the numbers could be anything, but they&#39;re still &#40;in my opinion&#41; true numbers.  I&#39;m leaning toward the idea that it&#39;s really an acronym for a sentence, and if that&#39;s the case, then &#34;V is for Victim&#34;, &#34;TBS&#34; is for &#34;The BTK Strangler&#34;, and the rest are unknown.  &#34;V14&#34;  sure looks to me like 14 victims.  I know it&#39;s just speculation, but so was DL, so I&#39;m trusting the simple stuff now.  Rader has not been coming clean on victims from the word go, but has been dribbling them out over a long period, as I would expect from somebody whose &#34;non-confessions&#34; should not be trusted.  He knows damn well how many he killed, and we know he&#39;s cocky about it on the inside, so I trust a &#34;14&#34;, left in a code he figured nobody could prove, a lot more than what he&#39;s not confessing to.  Short version - 10 my @$$.  He&#39;s easily good for 4 more, and his little puzzle is enough of a confession in my book that I think he should sweat for it until the numbers add up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10836-->
